# Backend Rules (`apps/api`)

Stack: NestJS, Better Auth (Bearer), Drizzle (`@elynd/db`), Zod (`@elynd/shared` / nestjs-zod), Vitest.

Placement and package boundaries: **`layering.mdc`** + **`decisions.mdc`** (framework-agnostic; follow those first).

Auth executable contracts: [`.trellis/spec/api/backend/auth-monorepo.md`](../../.trellis/spec/api/backend/auth-monorepo.md) when touching auth.

## TypeScript

- Extend `../../tsconfig.base.json`; keep Nest-only flags (`experimentalDecorators`, `emitDecoratorMetadata`, …) in this app's `tsconfig.json`
- Keep `outDir` / `rootDir` / `include` / `types` local
- **Imports (N1):** relative NodeNext imports with `.js` suffixes inside the API. Do **not** enable `@/` path aliases in emitted code until a Nest emit rewrite (e.g. `tsc-alias`) is added

## Layout (Nest mapping of layering)

| Folder | Role |
| ------ | ---- |
| `src/api/<feature>/` | Feature modules — business workflows |
| `src/auth/` | Auth feature / Better Auth wiring |
| `src/common/` | Transport cross-cutting: guards, pipes, filters, decorators — **no** domain workflows |
| `src/global/` | Global providers |
| `src/config/` | Env/config schemas |
| `src/core/` | App composition / core wiring only |

- Thin controllers: validate + map HTTP; business rules in injectable services
- Auth application logic via `AuthApplicationService` + `AuthClientPort` (mock the port in unit tests)
- Tech helpers with zero domain knowledge may live under `common/` or small dedicated folders — never import feature modules from tech helpers
- Do not use Adonis-style Access Token auth on the Nest path
- Lazy Better Auth via `getAuthInstance()` — never eager-init at import time

## Validation & OpenAPI

- Prefer shared Zod helpers from `@elynd/shared/schemas` (pagination, common shapes)
- Compose feature HTTP DTOs from `@elynd/db` drizzle-zod in the feature module (e.g. `examples.schema.ts`)
- Use project Zod validation pipe / Swagger helpers already in `src/common`
- Do not duplicate the same request/response schema in the web app — put cross-app contracts in `@elynd/shared`

## Env

Required auth-related keys: `DATABASE_URI`, `AUTH_SECRET`, `BETTER_AUTH_URL`, `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` (see `auth-env.schema.ts`).

## Lint

Root `eslint.config.mjs` (run via `pnpm lint` / `pnpm -w exec eslint apps/api`).
